## 4. Artifacts

### `espalier/maps/2026-08-05-notifications/tickets/002-channel.md` (rewritten in full)

```markdown
---
ticket: 002
title: Which delivery channel ships first
type: grilling
status: closed
blocked_by: [001]
claimed_by: junhanliu.dev@gmail.com
claimed_at: 2026-08-07T00:01:00Z
---

## Question

In-app only, email only, or both — and if both, which is the source of truth?

## Resolution

**In-app is the v1 channel and the permanent source of truth.** Every
notification from the three triggering events settled in
[001 — Which events trigger notifications](001-triggering-events.md) is
delivered in-app. Email is not in v1.

**Email ships later, and only as a batched daily digest.** Per-event email —
one send per notification, mirroring the in-app feed — is ruled out
permanently, not deferred. Any later email work must be a digest that
aggregates; a design that emits one email per event contradicts this
resolution and needs a new ticket to overturn it.

### Rationale

Users of the system being replaced already complain about its email volume,
and that complaint is the originating reason this epic exists. Mirroring
every in-app notification to email would reproduce the exact failure the
effort is meant to fix. Batching to a daily digest caps email volume at one
message per user per day regardless of event count, which is the property
that makes email safe to add at all.

Making in-app the source of truth (rather than a convenience view over an
email pipeline) keeps the digest a downstream read of notification state —
so digest behaviour can change without touching delivery.

### Citations

None — `espalier/rules/` and `espalier/wiki/` are empty in this repo, so the
grill's convention cross-check (Step 1.5) had nothing to check against and
skipped. This decision is not backed by an encoded convention; it is
user-stated product intent.
```

